--- Surface summary ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pure presentational port of the web ChargerTypeChart. The WinUI-free ChargerTypeChartProjection groups the
input sessions by charger category (web getChargerLabel: Supercharger / DC Fast / Home / AC, in first-seen
Map order), computes per-group avg kW (peak_power_w/1000), avg kWh (total_energy_added_wh/1000) and avg
duration (durationMinutes), and renders one of three web-derived branches:
  - Loading : title + skeleton chrome (parent still resolving the sessions).
  - Empty   : title + friendly empty surface (web ChartContainer chart.noData "No data available").
  - Ready   : two grouped bar series "Avg Power" (kW) / "Avg Energy" (kWh) via TsBarChart (native analogue of
              the recharts ComposedChart, no <Legend>), the per-charger-type legend list
              ("{count} sessions . {avgDuration} min avg", palette-by-index dots = native analogue of the web
              CHARGER_COLORS <Cell>), and the accessible Charger Type / Sessions / Avg kW / Avg kWh /
              Avg minutes data table (web ChartContainer dataColumns fallback).
No fetch-driven error/stale/offline branch exists in the presentational web source (the parent ChargingCurvePage
owns the query lifecycle) - same honest mapping as the sibling ChargerTypeBreakdown / MonthlyCostChart ports.
All 12 web t() keys flow through the ILocalizer facade (asserted by RecordingLocalizer test); diagnostics emit
"view.opened slug=ChargerTypeChart" (PII-safe). Native chart constraint documented honestly: the cartesian
surface shares one Y scale (the web uses split left/right kW/kWh axes) and tints bars per-series, so the exact
per-category figures live on the accessible table + tooltips and the charger-type colour lives on the legend.

